# Own-wording spells of Deep Magic (2014 rules), chunk I (Phantom Light to Scaly Hide). TEXT = {name: [summary, full]}.
TEXT = {
"Phantom Light": ["Touch an object under 10 feet on a side to make it glow for 1 hour. Only up to six chosen creatures can see the light.",
 "Touch, 1 hour. You touch one object that is less than 10 feet in every dimension. It sheds bright light in a 20-foot radius and dim light for another 20 feet, in any color you like. When you cast the spell, name up to six creatures. Only they can see the light or benefit from it. Covering the object with something opaque blocks the light. You can use an action to dismiss the spell."],
"Phase Bolt": ["A 100-foot line of force deals 5d8 force damage (Dexterity save for half). The bolt passes through the first object it meets.",
 "Self (100-foot line), instant. You focus loose energy into a crackling bolt 100 feet long and 5 feet wide. Each creature in the line takes 5d8 force damage, or half as much with a successful Dexterity save. The bolt passes through the first inanimate object in its path and creatures beyond it get no cover benefit from that object. A second object stops the bolt.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** Using a slot of 4th level or higher adds 1d8 damage per slot level above 3rd."],
"Pitfall": ["A pit swallows a Huge or smaller ground-bound target (Dexterity save). It drops out 20 feet up a round later for 6d6 bludgeoning damage.",
 "60 feet, 1 minute. A pit opens beneath a Huge or smaller creature you can see that has no flying speed. The pit is a doorway to an extradimensional space, not a plain hole. The target makes a Dexterity save or falls in, and the pit closes over it. At the end of your next turn a new portal opens 20 feet above where the pit was, and the creature drops out. It lands prone and takes 6d6 bludgeoning damage. If the target saved, you can use a bonus action on your turn to reopen the pit at any spot you can see within range. The spell ends once a creature has fallen through and taken damage, or when the duration runs out."],
"Plaguebearer": ["Touch a creature to make it immune to the effects of disease for 48 hours. It can still carry and spread diseases.",
 "Touch, 48 hours. The creature you touch suffers no effects from disease for the duration. It can still catch and carry diseases and pass them on, per the rules for that affliction. When exposed, it still makes the required save, and a failure makes it a carrier. It knows when it becomes infected. If it recovers or is cured of every disease it caught during the spell, the protection continues until the spell ends. When the spell ends, the creature becomes subject to any disease it still carries, as if it had just caught it.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** Using a slot of 3rd level or higher adds 24 hours per slot level above 2nd."],
"Poisoned Volley": ["Ghostly green arrows fill a 20-foot square within 60 feet. 3d8 poison damage and the poisoned condition (Constitution save for half and no poisoning).",
 "60 feet, instant. You draw back an imaginary bowstring and call up dozens of glowing green arrows. Every creature in a 20-foot square within range takes 3d8 poison damage and is poisoned. A creature that succeeds on a Constitution save takes half damage and is not poisoned.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** Using a slot of 3rd level or higher adds 1d8 damage per slot level above 2nd."],
"Poisonous Flesh": ["For 1 hour (concentration), creatures that bite you take 2d8 poison damage and are poisoned (Constitution save for half). Swallowing you is worse for them.",
 "Self, concentration, up to 1 hour. Your blood and flesh turn toxic to anything that would eat you. A creature that hits you with a bite attack makes a Constitution save. On a failure it takes 2d8 poison damage and is poisoned for 1 minute. On a success it takes half damage and is not poisoned. A creature with Intelligence 5 or higher will not willingly bite you again and looks for other prey. If it cannot break off combat, it uses other attacks when it can and bites you only when it has no other choice. If a creature swallows you, right after you take its digestion damage it takes 4d8 poison damage and is poisoned for 1 hour. A successful Constitution save negates the poisoned condition. On its next turn it uses an action to spit you out."],
"Portal Jaunt": ["Turn a door you can touch into a one-way portal to another door within 300 feet. You or one willing creature steps through before it closes.",
 "Touch, ritual, 300 feet, 1 round. You touch a prepared brass key to a door or gate and make it a one-way portal to another such opening within range. Any crafted door, doorway or archway works. Natural or accidental openings such as cave mouths or cracks do not. You must know the destination or be able to see it. When you finish casting, the touched door opens on a shimmering view of the far door. You can step through and come out of the destination door at once. You may instead let one other willing creature go through. Anything you carry goes with you, including other creatures, willing or not. For the spell's duration, locks, bars and magic such as arcane lock do not hinder the portal. You can reach only a side of the door that you can see or have visited (divination such as clairvoyance counts as seeing). When you or the willing creature has passed through, both doors shut and the spell ends. If nobody passes through within 1 round, the spell ends.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** Using a slot of 4th level or higher adds 100 feet to the range and 1 round to the duration per slot level above 3rd. Each added round lets one more creature use the portal before the spell ends."],
"Potency of the Pack": ["Grant a group within 25 feet one wolf trait for 1 minute: +2 AC, keen hearing and smell, or pack tactics.",
 "25 feet, 1 minute. You give wolflike traits to a group of living creatures you choose within range. Pick one benefit, and all targets gain it for the duration.\n\n**Thick Fur.** Each target grows fur over its whole body and gains a +2 bonus to AC.\n\n**Keen Hearing and Smell.** Each target has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing or smell.\n\n**Pack Tactics.** Each affected creature has advantage on an attack roll against a target if at least one of its allies who is also under this spell is within 5 feet of the target and is not incapacitated.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** Using a slot of 4th level or higher adds 1 minute to the duration per slot level above 3rd."],
"Power Word Kneel": ["Creatures within 20 feet of a point you pick kneel (prone) until they save. Affects up to 55 hit points of creatures, lowest first.",
 "60 feet, instant. You shout a word of power. Creatures within 20 feet of a point you choose are forced to kneel facing you, and a kneeling creature counts as prone. The spell affects up to 55 hit points of creatures, starting with those who have the fewest hit points. A kneeling creature makes a Wisdom save at the end of each of its turns and ends the effect on itself with a success. The effect ends at once on any creature that takes damage while kneeling."],
"Power Word Pain": ["One creature within 60 feet takes 4d10 force damage, then must keep saving on Constitution at each turn start or take another 4d10.",
 "60 feet, instant. You speak a word of power and one creature within 60 feet of you takes 4d10 force damage. At the start of each of its turns, it must make a Constitution save or take an extra 4d10 force damage. A successful save ends the effect."],
"Power Word Restore": ["Touch a construct to restore all its hit points, end all its negative conditions and let it stand up as a reaction.",
 "Touch, instant. You speak a word of power and energy flows over one construct you touch. It regains all of its lost hit points, every negative condition on it ends, and if it is prone it can use a reaction to stand up."],
"Prayer of Resolve": ["Up to six creatures within 30 feet gain temporary hit points equal to 1d10 plus your spellcasting modifier for 1 hour. No effect on undead or constructs.",
 "1 minute casting, 30 feet, 1 hour. You remind your allies of the endurance they will need. Each of up to six creatures you can see within range gains temporary hit points equal to 1d10 + your spellcasting ability modifier. The spell does nothing to undead or constructs. The temporary hit points last 1 hour.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** Using a slot of 3rd level or higher adds 1d10 to the temporary hit points each creature gains per slot level above 2nd."],
"Primal Infusion": ["Concentration, 1 minute. Gain 30 temporary hit points, pack advantage, +1d10 weapon damage, +2 AC and Constitution save proficiency.",
 "Self, concentration, up to 1 minute. You draw on the fury of nature. Until the spell ends you gain these benefits. You gain 30 temporary hit points, and any left when the spell ends are lost. You have advantage on attack rolls against a target if one of your allies is within 5 feet of it and that ally is not incapacitated. Your weapon attacks deal an extra 1d10 damage of the weapon's damage type on a hit. You gain a +2 bonus to AC. You are proficient in Constitution saving throws."],
"Prismatic Ray": ["Ranged spell attack within 100 feet. A d8 roll picks the color and its effect: 8d10 damage, or a condition for 5 rounds.",
 "100 feet, instant. A ray of shifting color leaps from your hand. Make a ranged spell attack against one creature you can see within range. Roll a d8 when the beam hits to see which color dominates.\n\n**1 Red.** 8d10 fire damage (Dexterity save).\n**2 Orange.** 8d10 acid damage (Dexterity save).\n**3 Yellow.** 8d10 lightning damage (Dexterity save).\n**4 Green.** Poisoned (Constitution save).\n**5 Blue.** Deafened (Constitution save).\n**6 Indigo.** Frightened (Wisdom save).\n**7 Violet.** Stunned (Constitution save).\n**8 Shifting ray.** Blinded (Constitution save).\n\nA damaging color deals half damage on a successful Dexterity save. For a condition, a successful Constitution or Wisdom save negates it. On a failed save the target is affected for 5 rounds or until the effect is negated. On a critical hit you pick the color of the beam, but the hit does no extra damage."],
"Proselytize": ["Creatures within 10 feet make a Wisdom save or are knocked prone and cannot take reactions until the end of their next turn.",
 "10-foot radius around you, instant. You fill your words with dread and darkness and drive nearby creatures to their knees. Every creature within 10 feet of you makes a Wisdom save. On a failure, it is knocked prone and cannot take reactions until the end of its next turn.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** Using a slot of 2nd level or higher adds 10 feet to the radius per slot level above 1st."],
"Protection from the Void": ["Touch a willing creature for 10 minutes (concentration). It resists necrotic and psychic damage and has advantage on saves against void spells.",
 "Touch, concentration, up to 10 minutes. The willing creature you touch has resistance to necrotic and psychic damage and advantage on saving throws against void spells until the spell ends. The material component is a small bar of silver worth 15 sp, which the spell consumes."],
"Protective Ice": ["Touch a willing creature to wrap it in icy armor (AC 14, 30 hit points) for 1 hour. Melee attackers within 5 feet take 1d6 cold damage.",
 "Touch, concentration, up to 1 hour. You encase a willing target in icy medium armor equal to a breastplate (AC 14). A creature without the proper armor proficiency takes the usual penalties. If the target already wears armor, it uses the better of the two Armor Classes. A creature that hits the target with a melee attack from within 5 feet takes 1d6 cold damage. If the wearer takes fire damage, the armor takes the same amount of damage. The armor has 30 hit points and is damaged only by fire damage dealt to its wearer. Damaged ice can be repaired by casting a spell that deals cold damage on it, point for point, but never beyond 30 points restored.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** With a 4th-level slot the spell creates splint armor (AC 17, 40 hit points). With a 5th-level slot it creates plate armor (AC 18, 50 hit points). The armor gains 10 hit points for each slot level above 5th, but its AC stays 18. With a slot of 4th level or higher, the armor also deals an extra 2 cold damage for each slot level above 3rd."],
"Protective Nimbus": ["For 10 minutes you glow with bright light in 20 feet (dim for another 20) and resist necrotic damage.",
 "Self, 10 minutes. You wrap yourself in a corona that sheds bright light in a 20-foot radius and dim light for an additional 20 feet. Until the spell ends, you have resistance to necrotic damage. You can end it early with an action."],
"Puff of Smoke": ["Bonus action cantrip. One creature within 30 feet makes a Dexterity save or is blinded until the start of your next turn.",
 "Bonus action, 30 feet, instant. You turn the air near a target into thick smoke with elemental fire. One creature you can see within range makes a Dexterity save. On a failure, it is blinded until the start of your next turn. Creatures with tremorsense or blindsight are unaffected."],
"Pummelstone": ["Cantrip. Ranged spell attack for 1d6 bludgeoning damage, and the target subtracts a d4 from its attacks and checks next turn.",
 "60 feet, instant. You conjure a fist-sized stone and hurl it at a target. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit, the target takes 1d6 bludgeoning damage. On its next turn, whenever the target makes an attack roll or ability check, it must roll a d4 and subtract the result. The damage rises to 2d6 at 5th level, 3d6 at 11th level and 4d6 at 17th level."],
"Pyroclasm": ["A lava geyser (5-foot radius, 40 feet high) erupts within 500 feet for 10d8 fire damage, then spreads a lava pool. Holding it for a full minute turns it to stone.",
 "500 feet, concentration, up to 1 minute. You point at the ground or a similar surface within range and a geyser of lava erupts. The geyser is a cylinder with a 5-foot radius and 40-foot height. Each creature in the cylinder when it erupts, and each creature there at the start of your turn, takes 10d8 fire damage, or half with a successful Dexterity save. A pool of lava forms at the geyser's base. It starts at the same size as the geyser, and at the start of each of your turns its radius grows by 5 feet. A creature in the pool (but not in the geyser) at the start of your turn takes 5d8 fire damage. A creature that leaves the pool has its speed halved and has disadvantage on Dexterity saves because of a hardening layer of lava. These penalties last until it uses an action to break the stone off. If you keep concentrating for the full minute, the geyser and pool harden into permanent nonmagical stone. A creature in either area when it hardens is restrained until the stone is broken away."],
"Quench": ["Put out all nonmagical fires in a 30-foot radius within 120 feet, test against fire spells, and deal 8d6 cold damage to fire elementals.",
 "120 feet, 30-foot radius, instant. You extinguish every nonmagical fire in a 30-foot radius around a point you choose. You can also snuff fire spells in the area. For each fire spell there, make a spellcasting ability check against DC 10 + that spell's level. On a success, that spell ends. Fire elementals in the area take 8d6 cold damage, or half with a successful Constitution save.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** Using a slot of 4th level or higher adds 10 feet to the radius and 1d6 to the damage against fire elementals per slot level above 3rd."],
"Quick Time": ["Age one creature or plant within 30 feet by one year. A creature with Intelligence 3 or higher may resist with a Constitution save.",
 "30 feet, instant. One living creature or plant within range moves rapidly through time. The target becomes one year older. For example, a seedling sprouts, or a newly hatched duckling becomes a full-grown duck. A creature with Intelligence 3 or higher must succeed on a Constitution save to resist, and it can choose to fail.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** Using a slot of 5th level or higher ages the target one extra year per slot level above 4th."],
"Quicken": ["Cantrip. A willing creature you touch can add a d4 to one initiative roll or Dexterity save before the spell ends.",
 "Touch, concentration, up to 1 minute. You touch one willing creature. Once before the spell ends, the target can roll a d4 and add it to its initiative roll or to a Dexterity save it has just made. It can roll the die before or after the d20. The spell then ends."],
"Quicksilver Mantle": ["Turn a cloak into a mirror-bright mantle for 1 hour: +2 AC, advantage on saves against gaze attacks, and a chance to deflect ray spells.",
 "Self, 1 hour. You turn an ordinary nonmagical cloak into a highly reflective silvery garment. The mantle gives you +2 AC and advantage on saving throws against gaze attacks. Whenever a ray such as ray of enfeeblement, scorching ray or disintegrate hits you, roll a d4. On a 4, the cloak deflects the ray and it strikes a random target within 10 feet of you instead. The cloak deflects only the first ray that hits it each round. Later rays affect you normally. The material components are the cloak and a dram of quicksilver worth 10 gp."],
"Quintessence": ["You take on angelic features for 1 minute: AC at least 20, immune to frightened and necrotic, and hostile creatures within 120 feet risk a frightened and restrained effect.",
 "Self (120-foot radius), concentration, up to 1 minute. You call on an archangel and are filled with celestial essence, gaining golden skin, shining eyes and ethereal wings. For the duration, your AC cannot be lower than 20, you cannot be frightened, and you are immune to necrotic damage. Each hostile creature that starts its turn within 120 feet of you, or enters that area for the first time on a turn, must succeed on a Wisdom save or be frightened for 1 minute. A creature frightened this way is also restrained. A frightened creature repeats the save at the end of each of its turns and ends the effect on itself on a success. A creature that succeeds on the save, or whose effect ends, is immune to this spell's frightening effect until you cast quintessence again."],
"Raid the Lair": ["10-foot protective field around you for 1 hour. Allies resist dragon lair actions: disadvantage on attacks, advantage and half damage on saves, later initiative.",
 "10 minutes casting, self, concentration, up to 1 hour. You make an invisible circle of protective energy with a 10-foot radius, centered on you and moving with you. You and all allies in the field are protected against a dragon's lair actions. Attack rolls that come directly from lair actions are made with disadvantage. Saving throws that come directly from lair actions are made with advantage, and the damage from those lair actions is halved. Lair actions occur on an initiative count 10 lower than normal. You have advantage on Constitution saves to maintain concentration on this spell."],
"Rain of Blades": ["Swords, spears and axes fall on a 150 square foot area within 25 feet for 4 rounds. 6d6 slashing damage (Dexterity save for half).",
 "25 feet, 4 rounds. You call down a rain of swords, spears and axes. The blades fill 150 square feet. That can be six 5-foot squares, a circle 15 feet across, or any contiguous pattern at least 5 feet wide everywhere. Each creature in the area when the spell is cast takes 6d6 slashing damage, or half with a successful Dexterity save. An intelligent undead harmed by the blades is frightened for 1d4 rounds if it fails a Charisma save. Most blades shatter or stick in the ground, but one piercing or slashing melee weapon can be salvaged from the area and used normally if claimed before the spell ends. When the duration ends, all the blades, including the salvaged one, vanish.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** Using a slot of 6th level or higher lets an unbroken blade be picked up and used as a magical +1 weapon until it disappears."],
"Raise Elder": ["Works like raise dead but only for someone who died of old age. They gain one more year of life but lose 2 Strength and 2 Constitution.",
 "Touch, 1 hour casting, instant. This spell is identical to raise dead, but it works only on a creature that died of old age. The raised elder gains one additional year of life. The creature has entirely white hair and weak eyes, and it loses 2 points each from Strength and Constitution. Nothing less potent than wish can restore those points. Otherwise it lives out its life normally until the extra year ends. The spell has no effect if cast on the same creature a second time. The material component is a diamond worth at least 1,000 gp, which the spell consumes."],
"Raise Ghost": ["Return a creature dead no longer than 10 days to an incorporeal form with 1 hit point. It cannot touch the world or cast spells, and has a -4 penalty that fades by 1 per long rest.",
 "Touch, 1 hour casting, instant. You return a dead creature you touch to a ghostly, incorporeal form, as long as it has been dead no more than 10 days. It can see and hear, and it can speak in a hollow tone if it chooses. Whether it wants to speak to you depends on its mood and past relationship with you. The creature is not undead. It is alive but incorporeal, with 1 hit point. It cannot interact with the physical world, attack, deal damage or cast spells. It is immune to nonmagical damage. It can pass through creatures and objects as if they were difficult terrain, but takes 1d10 force damage if it ends its turn inside an object. It regains hit points normally from resting or spending Hit Dice, but never from spells, items or potions. The spell also neutralizes any poison and cures nonmagical diseases that affected the creature when it died. It does not remove magical diseases, curses or similar effects. If those are not removed beforehand, they take hold when the creature returns to life. The spell closes mortal wounds but does not restore missing body parts. If the creature lacks organs or parts essential to survival, such as its head, the spell fails. Returning from death is an ordeal. The target has a -4 penalty to saving throws and ability checks. Each time it finishes a long rest, the penalty drops by 1 until it is gone. Raise dead or comparable magic restores a raised ghost to normal physical life. The spell has no effect on undead. The material component is a diamond worth at least 500 gp, which the spell consumes."],
"Raise Hero": ["Identical to raise dead, but the creature lives for only 24 hours. Recasting on the same creature risks failure on a d20 roll.",
 "Touch, 1 hour casting, 24 hours. This spell is identical to raise dead in every way except duration. The creature is restored to life for only 24 hours. You can recast the spell on the same creature, but for the second and later castings, you must roll a d20. If the roll is equal to or lower than the number of earlier castings on that creature, the spell fails and can never affect that creature again. Each new casting resets the clock to 24 hours. It does not add another 24 hours to the previous casting. The material component is a diamond worth at least 500 gp, which the spell consumes."],
"Raise Nemesis": ["Identical to raise dead, but it also raises a creature of opposite alignment within 100 miles. If either dies, the other drops dead.",
 "Touch, 1 hour casting, instant. This spell is identical to raise dead, except that it raises two creatures of opposite alignments at once. If you raise a Lawful Good paladin, a Chaotic Evil warrior of similar power also returns to life somewhere nearby. The second corpse must be within 100 miles. Both raised creatures have a vague sense of the direction and distance to their nemesis. They are not compelled to fight or seek each other. Their lives are bound together, though. If either dies, the other drops dead instantly. Evil NPCs raised this way usually see it as a chance to cause all kinds of trouble. If the spell is cast on a creature of true Neutral alignment, only that creature is restored to life. The material component is a diamond worth at least 500 gp, which the spell consumes."],
"Raise Questing Dead": ["Identical to raise dead, but you place a geas on the creature. It has 30 days to finish the task or it dies at dawn of day 31.",
 "Touch, 1 hour casting, instant. This spell is identical to raise dead, except that you can place a geas on the creature you raise. The soul can decline the geas, and if it does, it is not restored to life. If the creature accepts, it must complete the task within 30 days. If it accepts but fails to meet the geas conditions, it dies at dawn on the 31st day and its spirit leaves the mortal world again. If it completes the task, it is free to live out the rest of its restored life as it wishes. The material component is a diamond worth at least 500 gp, which the spell consumes."],
"Raise Shade": ["Identical to raise ghost, except the ghostly figure can manipulate, hold and carry objects up to 5 pounds.",
 "Touch, 1 hour casting, instant. This spell is identical to raise ghost in every way, except that the ghostly figure can manipulate, hold or carry objects weighing up to 5 pounds. That much force is enough to lift many melee weapons, but not enough to wield one in combat or to draw a bow. The material component is a diamond worth at least 500 gp, which the spell consumes."],
"Ravages of Time": ["One creature within 60 feet is aged to a decrepit state for 24 hours, suffering three levels of exhaustion that normal means cannot remove.",
 "60 feet, 24 hours. You speed the aging of one creature within range, leaving it a decrepit version of its kind. The target suffers three levels of exhaustion that cannot be removed by normal means. Greater restoration partly reverses the spell, removing one level of exhaustion. Constructs and undead are unaffected, as are creatures that live to great age without ill effect, such as dragons."],
"Ray of Alchemical Negation": ["Ranged spell attack within 60 feet destroys alchemical reagents in an item or trap, or deals 6d6 force damage to alchemical creatures and halves their alchemical attack damage.",
 "60 feet, instant. You fire a ray of blazing, many-colored energy from your fingertips. Make a ranged spell attack against an alchemical item or a trap that works through alchemy, such as one that sprays acid, releases poison gas or sets off alchemist's fire. A hit destroys the reagents and makes them harmless. The attack is made against the most suitable object AC. You can also target a creature within range that is wholly or partly made of acidic, poisonous or alchemical components, such as an alchemical golem or an ochre jelly. On a hit, it takes 6d6 force damage and must succeed on a Constitution save or deal only half damage with its acidic, poisonous or alchemical attacks for 1 minute. A creature with halved damage repeats the save at the end of each of its turns and ends the effect on a success."],
"Ray of Life Suppression": ["Ranged spell attack within 60 feet deals 6d8 necrotic damage and cuts the target's maximum hit points by the same amount. No effect on constructs or undead.",
 "60 feet, instant. You launch a swirling ray of disruptive energy at a creature within range. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit, the creature takes 6d8 necrotic damage and its hit point maximum is reduced by the same amount. The reduction lasts until the creature finishes a short or long rest, or until it benefits from greater restoration or comparable magic. The spell has no effect on constructs or undead."],
"Read Memory": ["Spend 10 minutes to copy the memories stored in a gearforged's memory gear into your own mind, without emotional context.",
 "Self, 10 minutes casting, instant. You copy the memories held in one memory gear into your own mind. You recall them as if you had lived them, but without any emotional attachment or context. The material component is a memory gear from a gearforged."],
"Read Object": ["Handle an object for 1 minute (concentration) and the GM may give one piece of information about its history each round.",
 "Touch, 1 minute casting, concentration, up to 1 minute. By holding an object and reading the psychic residue on it, you can learn about its past. After casting, you keep holding the object and read the impressions it carries. Each round, the GM may give you one piece of information about the item's ownership and handling. The GM may decide an item has too little residue to give any clear impression. Examples of information you might gain: the item's name, if it has one. A visual image of the last creature to handle it. The emotional state of the creature that last used it. If it is or was used as a weapon, an image of the last creature it injured or killed. A visual image of its owner or maker. Facts about its historical importance, if any."],
"Reaver Spirit": ["You and allies within 30 feet gain advantage on Strength checks and saves, resistance to nonmagical weapon damage and +2 melee damage for 1 minute. Afterward each must save or gain exhaustion.",
 "30 feet, concentration, up to 1 minute. You inspire allies to fight with the savagery of berserkers. You and any allies you can see within range have advantage on Strength checks and Strength saves, resistance to bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage from nonmagical attacks, and a +2 bonus to damage with melee weapons. When the spell ends, each affected creature must succeed on a Constitution save or gain 1d4 levels of exhaustion.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** Using a slot of 4th level or higher adds 1 to the damage bonus per slot level above 3rd."],
"Recharge": ["Touch a charged magic item to restore 1d3 charges. Overcharging an item that can make a retributive strike makes it explode.",
 "Touch, instant. You pull magical energy through yourself as a conduit to recharge a magic item. One magic item that uses charges and that you are touching regains 1d3 charges at once. An item cannot go above its maximum charges, and excess energy dissipates harmlessly, unless the item can make a retributive strike. If such an item is charged past its capacity, it explodes as if you had used an action to perform the retributive strike, with all its normal effects. The material component is a diamond worth at least 250 gp, which is consumed during the casting.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** Using a slot of 6th level or higher restores 1 extra charge per slot level above 5th."],
"Remove Scent": ["Strip odors from a 40-foot cube, or give one Large or smaller creature or object no scent for an hour.",
 "30 feet, instant. You magically remove strong odors from an area, a person or an object. The target can be a cube up to 40 feet on a side, or a single creature or object of Large size or smaller. A room full of garbage or carrion stops smelling, or someone sprayed by a skunk loses the stench. If something there still produces odor, the smell returns within an hour. If cast in the area of a stinking cloud, it removes the odor and the spell's nauseating effect, but not the fog itself. You can also cast it on one creature of Large size or smaller that does not already give off a strong odor, such as a troglodyte. For the next hour, that creature has no scent and cannot be found by Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on scent."],
"Repair Metal": ["Touch a damaged construct or metal object to restore 1d8 + 5 hit points.",
 "Touch, instant. A damaged construct or metal object regains 1d8 + 5 hit points when you cast this spell on it.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The spell restores 2d8 + 10 hit points at 4th level, 3d8 + 15 at 6th level and 4d8 + 20 at 8th level."],
"Reposition": ["Bonus action. Up to three friendly creatures within 30 feet (you may be one) each teleport to an unoccupied space they can see within 30 feet.",
 "Bonus action, 30 feet, instant. You choose up to three friendly creatures within range, and you can be one of them. Each target teleports to an unoccupied space of its choice that it can see within 30 feet of itself.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** Using a slot of 5th level or higher targets one extra friendly creature per slot level above 4th."],
"Reset": ["Up to four creatures within 60 feet. Allies may reroll initiative twice and keep the better result. Enemies must save or reroll as you prefer.",
 "60 feet, instant. Temporal energy bursts from you across the battlefield. Choose up to four creatures within range. An ally can reroll its initiative twice and keep whichever result it prefers. An enemy must succeed on a Wisdom save or reroll its initiative twice, keeping whichever result you prefer. The new initiative results take effect at the start of the next round.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** Using a slot of 5th level or higher affects one extra creature per slot level above 4th."],
"Reverberate": ["A 15-foot cone from you shakes the ground. 4d6 thunder damage and prone (Dexterity save for half and no prone).",
 "Self (15-foot cone), instant. You strike the ground with a metal ring and send a shock through the earth ahead of you. Creatures and unattended objects touching the ground in a 15-foot cone from you take 4d6 thunder damage and creatures fall prone. A successful Dexterity save halves the damage and prevents a creature from falling prone.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** Using a slot of 3rd level or higher adds 1d6 damage per slot level above 2nd."],
"Revive Beast": ["Touch a beast that died within the last minute to return it to life with 1 hit point. It cannot fix old age or missing parts.",
 "Touch, instant. You touch a beast that died in the last minute, and it returns to life with 1 hit point. The spell cannot revive a beast that died of old age, and it does not restore missing body parts. The material component is emeralds worth 100 gp, which the spell consumes."],
"Right the Stars": ["10-minute ritual. For 1 hour your conjuration durations double, your summons get 30 temporary hit points and you have advantage on Charisma checks and saves.",
 "Self, 10 minutes casting, 1 hour. You gently bend space and time to power up your conjurations with cosmic force. Until the spell ends, the maximum duration of any concentration conjuration spell you cast is doubled. Any creature you summon or create with a conjuration spell has 30 temporary hit points. You have advantage on Charisma checks and Charisma saving throws. The material components are seven black candles and a circle of powdered charred bone or basalt."],
"Ring Strike": ["Infuse two metal rings that orbit you for 1 hour. When you hit a target within 60 feet, launch a ring for 1d10 bludgeoning damage and a Strength save or a 5-foot push.",
 "Self, 1 hour. You infuse two metal rings with magic so they circle slowly around your head or hand. For the duration, when you hit a target within 60 feet of you with an attack, you can launch one ring to strike that target too. The target takes 1d10 bludgeoning damage and must succeed on a Strength save or be pushed 5 feet straight away from you. The ring is destroyed when it strikes.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** Using a slot of 2nd level or higher lets you affect two additional rings per slot level above 1st."],
"Ring Ward": ["An iron ring becomes a 15-foot-radius circle of energy around you for 1 hour. You and allies inside have advantage on saves against spells and resist one damage type you choose.",
 "Self, concentration, up to 1 hour. The iron ring you use in the casting becomes a faintly shimmering circlet of energy that spins slowly around you at a 15-foot radius. For the duration, you and your allies inside the protected area have advantage on saving throws against spells, and all affected creatures gain resistance to one damage type of your choice. The material component is an iron ring worth 200 gp, which the spell consumes."],
"Ringstrike": ["Infuse up to two metal rings that orbit you for 1 hour. When you hit a target within 120 feet, launch a ring for 1d10 bludgeoning damage and a Strength save or a 5-foot push.",
 "120 feet, 1 hour. You infuse up to two metal rings with magic so they circle slowly around your head or hand. For the duration, when you hit a target within range with an attack, you can launch one ring to strike that target too. The target takes 1d10 bludgeoning damage and must succeed on a Strength save or be pushed 5 feet straight away from you. The ring is destroyed when it strikes. The spell consumes a metal ring for each strike it grants.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** Using a slot of 2nd level or higher lets you affect two additional rings per slot level above 1st."],
"Ringward": ["An iron ring becomes a 15-foot-radius circle of energy around you for 1 hour. You and allies inside have advantage on saves against spells and resist one damage type you choose.",
 "Self, concentration, up to 1 hour. The iron ring you cast with becomes a faintly shimmering circle of energy that spins slowly around you at a 15-foot radius. For the duration, you and your allies inside the energy ring have advantage on saving throws against spells and gain resistance to one damage type of your choice. The material component is an iron ring worth 200 gp, which the spell consumes."],
"Riptide": ["A 20-foot-tall, 20-foot-radius water cylinder restrains creatures (Strength save). Next turn, sweep them away for 3d8 bludgeoning damage or drag them down and stun them.",
 "60 feet, 1 round. With a sweeping gesture you raise water into a cylinder 20 feet tall with a 20-foot radius, centered on a point on the ground you can see. Each creature in the cylinder makes a Strength save. On a failure, it is restrained and held in the cylinder. On a success, it moves to just outside the nearest edge. At the start of your next turn, as the swell fades, you steer the current and choose one option.\n\n**Riptide.** The water flows in a direction you choose and sweeps along each creature in the cylinder. An affected creature takes 3d8 bludgeoning damage and is pushed 40 feet in that direction, landing prone.\n\n**Undertow.** The water rushes downward and drags each creature in the cylinder into an unoccupied space at the center. Each is knocked prone and must succeed on a Constitution save or be stunned until the start of your next turn."],
"Roaming Pain": ["A humanoid within 30 feet suffers pain in a random body part each round (d6 table). It saves with Constitution each turn to ignore it. Concentration, 1 minute.",
 "30 feet, concentration, up to 1 minute. You afflict one humanoid within range with severe pain that shifts to random parts of its body. At the start of the target's turn each round, roll on the table to see where the pain strikes. The target then makes a new Constitution save. On a success, it functions despite the pain and ignores the effect that round. If the target succeeds against the pain in a particular area, it also automatically succeeds against pain in that same area on later turns.\n\n**1 Head.** Incapacitated.\n**2 Throat.** Unable to speak coherently or cast spells with verbal components.\n**3 Chest.** Cannot take reactions or bonus actions.\n**4 Abdomen.** Disadvantage on Constitution saving throws.\n**5 Arm.** Disadvantage on attack rolls and on Strength and Dexterity ability checks.\n**6 Leg.** Movement halved."],
"Roaring Winds of Limbo": ["A storm of chaos fills twelve 10-foot cubes within 150 feet. Creatures are deafened, shoved by wind, slowed, and you can pelt up to twelve with 2d10 bludgeoning, piercing and slashing debris each.",
 "150 feet, concentration, up to 1 minute. You tear open a breach to the planes of chaos, and a dangerous windstorm fills the area. The area is twelve 10-foot cubes arranged as you like, and each cube must share a face with another. Each creature in the area is deafened, and no sound it makes can be heard outside the area. The wind scatters gases and vapors and snuffs unprotected flames in the area. It has a 75 percent chance to put out protected flames such as lanterns. All Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight made by a creature in the area have disadvantage because of dust and debris. Each creature in the area makes a Strength save at the start of its turn. On a failure, it is pushed 15 feet in a random direction (roll a d8, with 1 as north, 2 as northeast, 3 as east, and so on around the compass). The wind also hampers movement. A creature in the area spends 2 feet of movement for every 1 foot it moves. As a bonus action on each of your turns, you can hurl flying debris at up to twelve creatures in the area. Each takes 2d10 bludgeoning, 2d10 piercing and 2d10 slashing damage, or half as much with a successful Dexterity save."],
"Robe of Shards": ["For 1 minute, a robe of metal gives base AC 14 + Dexterity. Absorb scrap to raise AC up to 18 + Dexterity, or burst it for 8d6 slashing damage in 30 feet.",
 "Self, 1 minute. You create a robe of metal shards, gears and cogs that gives you a base AC of 14 + your Dexterity modifier. As a bonus action while wearing it, you can have it absorb bits of metal from a fallen foe. Each infusion raises your AC by 1, to a maximum of 18 + your Dexterity modifier. You can also use a bonus action to dispel the robe, and it explodes in a shower of flying metal. All creatures within 30 feet take 8d6 slashing damage, plus 1d6 for each point of base (non-Dexterity) AC above 14."],
"Rolling Thunder": ["A 30-foot by 5-foot line of sound. Creatures make a Constitution save or are deafened for 1 minute, taking 2d8 thunder damage each turn and moving at half speed.",
 "Self (30-foot line), instant. A huge bell note bursts from your outstretched hand and rolls forward in a line 30 feet long and 5 feet wide. Each creature in the line must succeed on a Constitution save or be deafened for 1 minute. A creature made of stone, crystal, metal or similar material has disadvantage on the save. While deafened this way, a creature is wreathed in thundering energy. It takes 2d8 thunder damage at the start of its turn and its speed is halved. A deafened creature repeats the save at the end of each of its turns and ends the effect on itself on a success.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** Using a slot of 3rd level or higher adds 1d8 damage per slot level above 2nd."],
"Rotting Corpse": ["Touch a creature that died in the last 24 hours to keep it from being raised by raise dead for 3 days. After that it rots to slime and only true resurrection works.",
 "Touch, 10 minutes casting, 3 days. You use your knowledge of death's foul effects to keep a body from being returned to life by anything but the most powerful magic. Touch a creature that died within the last 24 hours. The body decays at once to a state in which raise dead cannot restore it, though resurrection still works. At the end of the duration, the body rots to rancid slime and can only be returned to life by true resurrection.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** Using a slot of 3rd level or higher affects one extra corpse per slot level above 2nd."],
"Rune of Imprisonment": ["Ranged spell attack within 30 feet traps a creature inside a glowing rune for up to 1 minute (concentration). An adjacent creature can try to free it, giving a Wisdom save.",
 "30 feet, concentration, up to 1 minute. You trace a glowing black rune in the air and it streaks toward the target and envelops it. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit, the rune absorbs the creature, leaving only the glowing rune in the space the creature occupied. The prisoner can take no actions, and it cannot be targeted or affected by any means. Spell durations and conditions on it are postponed until it is freed. A dying creature neither loses hit points nor stabilizes until freed. A creature next to the rune can use an action to try to disrupt its energies. When it does, the imprisoned creature makes a Wisdom save. On a success, the disruption cancels the imprisonment and ends the effect. Disruption can be attempted only once per round."],
"Sacrificial Healing": ["Touch a creature and roll 4d8. It heals that amount and you (or another willing creature in range) take the same damage.",
 "Touch, instant. You heal another creature's wounds by taking them on yourself, or by moving them to another willing creature in range. Roll 4d8. The target heals that many hit points as its wounds close, and similar damage appears on your body (or on the other willing target)."],
"Salt Lash": ["Conjure a salt-crystal blade for 10 minutes (concentration). Attack with your spellcasting modifier for 2d8 slashing damage and a stun (Constitution save).",
 "Self, concentration, up to 10 minutes. You create a long thin blade of razor-sharp salt crystals. You wield it as a longsword, adding your spellcasting ability modifier to the weapon attack rolls. It deals 2d8 slashing damage on a hit, and a creature it hits must succeed on a Constitution save or be stunned by searing pain until the start of your next turn. Constructs and undead are immune to the stun. Plants and creatures made mostly of water, such as a water elemental, also take an extra 2d8 necrotic damage if they fail the save. The spell lasts until you stop concentrating, the duration ends, or you let go of the blade for any reason. The material component is a pinch of salt worth 1 sp, which is consumed during the casting."],
"Sand Ship": ["Make a ship up to the size of a small sailing ship able to sail on sand at normal speed for 24 hours.",
 "30 feet, 1 minute casting, 24 hours. You cast this on a water vessel up to the size of a small sailing ship and make it able to sail on sand as easily as on water. It still needs a trained crew and wind or oars to move, but it travels at its normal speed over sand instead of water for the duration. It can sail only over sand, not soil or bare rock. While the spell lasts, the vessel does not float. It must be beached or resting on the bottom of a body of water, for example partly drawn up on a beach, when you cast the spell, or it sinks. The material component is a boat or ship worth 10,000 gp or less."],
"Sanguine Horror": ["Prick yourself for 1 piercing damage to conjure a friendly blood elemental for 1 hour (concentration). If you lose concentration it turns hostile.",
 "5 feet, concentration, up to 1 hour. You prick yourself with the material component and take 1 piercing damage. The spell fails if that damage is prevented or negated in any way. From the drop of blood, you conjure a blood elemental. It is friendly to you and your companions for the duration, and it vanishes when reduced to 0 hit points or when the spell ends. Roll initiative for it, since it takes its own turns. It obeys your verbal commands, which take no action from you. If you give no commands, it defends itself and takes no other actions. If your concentration is broken, the blood elemental does not vanish. You lose control of it and it becomes hostile to you and your companions. You cannot dismiss an uncontrolled blood elemental, and it disappears 1 hour after you summoned it. The material component is a miniature dagger."],
"Scale Rot": ["One creature with natural armor within 30 feet makes a Constitution save. On a failure, attacks against it have advantage and it cannot regain hit points. It can repeat the save each turn.",
 "30 feet, concentration, up to 1 minute. You call down death and decay on your enemies. For dragons, this often means attacking a foe's armor and scales, but it works on any armored creature. One creature of your choice within range that has natural armor makes a Constitution save. On a failure, attacks against its Armor Class have advantage, and it cannot regain hit points by any means while the spell lasts. An affected creature can end the spell on itself by succeeding on a Constitution save at the end of its turn. A successful save also makes it immune to further castings of scale rot for 24 hours.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** Using a slot of 5th level or higher affects one extra target per slot level above 4th."],
"Scaly Hide": ["Touch a creature for 10 minutes (concentration). Its AC cannot be lower than 16 and it resists acid, cold, fire, lightning or poison, chosen at casting.",
 "Touch, concentration, up to 10 minutes. A creature you touch grows a protective layer of dragonlike scales. Until the spell ends, the target's AC cannot be lower than 16, whatever armor it wears. It also gains resistance to one of these damage types for the duration: acid, cold, fire, lightning or poison. The material component is a dragon scale of the matching color."],
}
